@startuml vss-transformer-states
title VssDataTransformer — Lifecycle

[*] --> LoadConfig

state "Load config.yaml" as LoadConfig
state "Spawn tasks" as Spawn

LoadConfig --> Spawn : config valid
LoadConfig --> [*] : config invalid → fail fast

state "KUKSA subscriber (background task)" as KuksaSide {
  state "Connect\nValClient::connect" as Dial
  state "Subscribe\nconfigured paths" as Sub
  state "Listen\nawait next pushed message" as Listen
  state "Process update\nextract → transform → cache" as Process
  state "Backoff\n1s → 2s → 4s ... capped at 30s" as Backoff

  Dial --> Sub : connected
  Sub --> Listen : stream open +\ncurrent values arrive immediately
  Listen --> Process : message pushed
  Process --> Listen : back to sleep
  Dial --> Backoff : connect failed
  Sub --> Backoff : subscribe failed
  Listen --> Backoff : stream closed / dropped
  Backoff --> Dial : retry
}

state "REST API (foreground)" as RestSide {
  state "Listening on :8080" as Serve
  state "Handle request" as Handle

  Serve --> Handle : GET /signals/{path}
  Handle --> Serve : 200 / 404 / 503
}

Spawn --> Dial
Spawn --> Serve

note right of Process
  e.g. Vehicle.Speed = 100 km/h
  × 0.621371
  → 62.1371 mph stored in cache
end note

note right of Handle
  path not configured → 404
  no value received yet → 503
  value cached → 200 + JSON
  (memory read only —
  never calls KUKSA)
end note

note bottom of Backoff
  While disconnected the cache
  keeps serving the last known value.
  The two sides are independent.
end note

@enduml

@startuml vss-query-flow
title Query flow

|Client CLI|
start
:vss-client --path Vehicle.Speed;
:build URL + send HTTP GET;

|Transformer :8080|
:route matches /signals/{path};
if (path configured?) then (no)
  :404 + list of known paths;
  detach
else (yes)
  if (value in cache?) then (no)
    :503 "no value yet";
    detach
  else (yes)
    :read cache under read-lock;
    :serialize to JSON;
    :200 OK;
  endif
endif

|Client CLI|
:print value to stdout;
stop

@enduml
